<p>There are three species of iris in the dataset: <em>setosa</em>, <em>versicolor</em>, and <em>virginica</em>. The records, which are <a href="https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/53/iris">easy to find</a>, are sorted according to class, and it’s necessary to randomize the records for certain operations.</p>
<p>Let’s say the measurements are in a 2D (150×4) NumPy array called <code>x</code>, and the classes, which have been reduced to the integers 0, 1, and 2 for <em>setosa</em>, <em>versicolor</em>, and <em>virginica</em>, respectively, are in a 1D NumPy array called <code>y</code>. Here they are in an interactive Python session:</p>
